        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Trix',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Trix (Trex) is a popular Middle Eastern compendium card game for 4 players. Each player 'owns a kingdom' of 5 contracts, choosing the order. 4 contracts are trick-avoidance (avoid Kâ™¥, Queens, Diamonds, or Tricks). The 5th contract 'Trix' is a shedding game where players play to a layout starting from Jacks. 20 deals total (4 kingdoms x 5 contracts).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trix (also spelled Trex or Ticks) is a compendium card game popular across the Levant and Gulf, including Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Palestine, Saudi Arabia, Syria and the United Arab Emirates. English-language rules were first documented from contributors in the region (Suad Harms, V M and others) in 2007. The game combines four trick-avoidance contracts with a fifth shedding contract similar to Fan Tan.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52. A(high)-2(low).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, score sheet',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '13 cards each. 7â™¥ holder owns first kingdom.',
              },
            ],
          },
